TITLE:: URI
summary:: Uniform Resource Identifier conversions
categories:: HelpSystem, IDE
related:: Classes/String, Classes/WebView

DESCRIPTION::

A representation of the Uniform Resource Identifier (URI).
This class attempts compliance with specification link::http://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/rfc3986/##Generic Syntax (RFC 3986)::.
Use it to construct a valid URIs from local paths and existing URLs.


CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Create a new URI instance from a valid URI string.

returns:: an instance of URI

METHOD:: fromLocalPath

Convert file path into a URI.

METHOD:: tolerant

Create a new URI instance, accepting both URLs and local paths as input.




INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: asString

returns:: the URI as a string

METHOD:: asLocalPath

returns:: A file path string, e.g. code::"/path/to/file.txt":: on *nix or code::c:\file\to\path.txt:: on Windows.

METHOD:: scheme

returns:: The Scheme component of the URI, like code::"https://":: or code::"file:///"::.

METHOD:: authority

returns:: The Authority component of the URI, i.e. the hostname. Typically the server name for URLs, empty for local file paths.

METHOD:: path

returns:: The Path segment of the URI, pointing to the local file. Typically empty for URLs.

METHOD:: fragment

returns:: The Fragment component of the URI, like a link to a section of a document.

METHOD:: query

returns:: The Query component of the URI, typically indicated after code::"?":: in the URI string.

PRIVATE:: init


EXAMPLES::

code::
u = URI("https://example.com?query=1#section");
u.dump; // inspect elements

p = URI("file:///path/to/file.txt");
p.dump;

// conversion from local paths
URI.fromLocalPath("/path/to/file.txt").asString; // returns "file:///path/to/file.txt"
URI.tolerant("/path/to/file.txt").asString; // the same as above, but can accept URLs transparently

"/path/to/file.txt".pathToURI; // shorthand for Strings


::
